 ## Overview
-Cartoon Noise Lattice Generation produces independent, tileable noise lattices for stylized, cartoon-style cloud rendering by separating noise into four distinct functional groups: macro (outline), body (fill), edge (detail), and flow (disturbance) [S1, unofficial]. The method generates multiple specialized lattices with specific frequency constraints to ensure stability and avoid fixed-direction ripple artifacts, building on [Gradient-based Noise (Perlin/Simplex)](3860-gradient-based-noise-perlin-simplex.md) [S1, unofficial].
